MUTANTS (mutants_13a.py, repair 14's latch_label() verbatim, label swapped):
  M7_intmasklatch  latch SET + narrow access at CRIME_INTMASK (0x018) falls through to `crime_interrupt_reassert(d)'
  M8_ctllatch      latch SET + narrow access at CRIME_CONTROL (0x008) falls through to the CONTROL arm

PREDICTIONS (per row; CHANNEL = the observable that differs under the mutant):

  base              204/204, FAILING: none.

  M7_intmasklatch   KILLED, exactly 201/204.
    reds  imask sb   CHANNEL: cause IP2 printed after `sb +0x18 0xff' -- the arm reasserts with INTMASK = SOFTINT = BIT
                     (stored by the two accepted sd), so IP2 goes SET; the row wants clear.
          imask lh   same channel, the next `print cause' (IP2 stays set: nothing deasserts it).
          imask sh   same channel, the next `print cause'.
    green imask pre / imask lb (lb +0x18 is the session's FIRST refusal: declined, latch set) / imask ctl (wants set) /
          imask once, said (one announce) / imask lb v0, lh v0 (the width arm is skipped either way: answers 0) /
          imask keeps (no store lands: INTMASK stays BIT).  The istat session refuses at 0x10 only: unaffected.
    Reads at +0x18 elsewhere: none after a latch in any other session.

  M8_ctllatch       KILLED.  Certain reds: sb08 msg, sh08b run, gate run.  Possible reds: gate lb v0, gate lh v0.
    reds  sb08 msg   CHANNEL: the CONTROL arm's `unimplemented control' text.  `sb 0x01' is the first refusal (declined);
                     `sb 0xff' falls through with idata 0xff: no DOG, no RESET, ENDIANESS clear -> 0xff != 0 -> fatal().
          sh08b run  CHANNEL: the RAM trip's v1.  `sh 0x0201' first (declined); `sh 0x0900' falls through with
                     HARD_RESET (0x800) set -> every CPU's running = 0 -> the roundtrip never runs.
          gate run   CHANNEL: v1.  `lb +0x08' first (declined); `lh +0x08' falls through as a READ (the arm does nothing
                     on reads: answers 0, green); `sh 0x0800' falls through with HARD_RESET -> CPUs stop.
    possible  gate lb v0 / gate lh v0: their `print t1' / `print s3' come AFTER the stopping store; if the emulator
                     ends when every CPU stops, the prints never happen and both read absent (red).  Not predicted
                     either way -- it depends on what the debugger does with no running CPU, which I have not read.
    green sh08 run/pc (`sh 0x0800' is that session's FIRST refusal: declined) / sb08 run (0xff stops nothing) /
          sh08b msg (0x0900 is cleared to 0 by the arm; the 0xffff store never runs once the CPUs stop) /
          sh08b once, said / dog-session ctl v0, ctl lb v0 (READS at +0x08: the arm does nothing on a read; answers 0).
    Score: at most 201/204 (three certain reds), at least 199/204.

